course: dictionary
lesson: 2623
title: Descriptions: words that paint a picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A description is a set of words that tells you what someone or something is like: how it looks, sounds, feels or behaves. A good description helps you picture a person or place in your head.
explain: «Descriptions of a place can tell you about the people, like a weedy garden and a broken gate suggesting nobody cares for the house.» The words never say the owners are careless, but the weeds and the broken gate are clues that hint at it.
explain: Description can also mean the act of describing, which is telling someone what something is like. «Explorers travelled into the unknown and brought back descriptions, so mapmakers could fill in the gaps bit by bit.»
fact: A description is words that tell what someone or something is like.
fact: Description can also mean the act of describing.
fact: «Give a description» means tell someone what a person or thing looks, sounds or feels like.
fact: «Fit the description» means match the details that were described.
fact: A clue is a detail in the text, like an action or a description, that hints at something.
exercise: «Descriptions of a place can tell you about the people.» What is a description? | A kind of race you run in a park | A loud noise made by a door | *Words that tell what someone or something is like | A number that counts the rooms
exercise: Mum says, «Give a description of the thief.» What should you do? | Tell your favourite film | Say nothing at all | Hide the thief behind the sofa | *Tell her what the thief looked like
exercise: «A clue is a detail in the text, like an action or a description, that hints at something.» What is a clue? | A loud noise | A full stop at the end of a sentence | *A detail that hints at something
test: Ella's teacher says, «Write a description of the castle.» What should Ella write? | A list of her homework | A shopping list for the trip | *Words that tell what the castle looks, sounds and feels like | A sum about castles
test: «Picture-making AI learned from millions of pictures with descriptions.» What did the AI learn from? | Only from songs | Only from maps of the moon | Nothing at all, it guessed | *Pictures that came with descriptions
exam: «A description made only of famous things everyone knows, with nothing personal, may come from films rather than memory.» What does this sentence suggest? | Everyone remembers the same thing | Films always show true memories | Personal descriptions are always false | *A description with nothing personal may have been copied from films
